{"content":"q19. MemoService is served over two protocols, both wired up in `server/router/api/v1/v1.go`:\n\n1. **gRPC-Gateway (REST/JSON transcoding of gRPC)** — registered via `v1pb.RegisterMemoServiceHandlerServer(ctx, gwMux, s)` inside `RegisterGateway`, `server/router/api/v1/v1.go:108`. This mux is then mounted at `/api/v1/*` (`server/router/api/v1/v1.go:128`).\n\n2. **Connect-RPC (used for browser clients, replacing grpc-web)** — wrapped via `apiv1connect.NewMemoServiceHandler(s, opts...)` inside `RegisterConnectHandlers`, `server/router/api/v1/connect_handler.go:40`. That handler is invoked from `v1.go:141` (`connectHandler.RegisterConnectHandlers(...)`) and mounted at `/memos.api.v1.*` (`server/router/api/v1/v1.go:144`).\n\nSo:\n- gRPC-Gateway — `server/router/api/v1/v1.go`\n- Connect-RPC — `server/router/api/v1/connect_handler.go`\n\n(Note: a plain native-gRPC `RegisterMemoServiceServer`/`grpc.ServiceRegistrar` generated stub exists at `proto/gen/api/v1/memo_service_grpc.pb.go:439`, but I found no call site wiring it into a `grpc.NewServer` — the two protocols actually served by the running server are the gRPC-Gateway and Connect handlers above.)","iteration":19,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
